1
00:00:42,355 --> 00:00:46,067
‎SPOOKY IN LOVE

2
00:00:51,239 --> 00:00:53,867
‎EMERGENCY SERVICES

3
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:04,961
‎Female in her thirties,
‎car accident victim.

4
00:01:05,044 --> 00:01:06,629
‎We found her unconscious

5
00:01:06,713 --> 00:01:08,506
‎with an initial blood pressure
‎of 100 over 80.

6
00:01:08,590 --> 00:01:11,509
‎Now it's 80 over 56 and falling.

7
00:01:14,888 --> 00:01:15,805
‎Mr. Ma.

8
00:01:17,432 --> 00:01:18,892
‎-Mr. Ma!
‎-What's wrong?

9
00:01:18,975 --> 00:01:20,310
‎-What's happening?
‎-Mr. Ma.

10
00:01:20,393 --> 00:01:21,895
‎-Is he okay?
‎-He needs help!

11
00:01:22,395 --> 00:01:25,106
‎-Mr. Ma, what's wrong?
‎-What's wrong, Gang-uk?

12
00:01:28,860 --> 00:01:30,194
‎I need more suction.

13
00:01:35,658 --> 00:01:36,993
‎Keep them coming.

14
00:01:37,076 --> 00:01:38,578
‎-Anesthesiologist, what's her BP?
‎-Yes?

15
00:01:38,661 --> 00:01:42,206
‎-It's stable at 100 over 60.
‎-Suction.

16
00:01:42,832 --> 00:01:44,417
‎-Keep an eye on the BP.
‎-Will do.

17
00:01:45,251 --> 00:01:46,210
‎I need more suction.

18
00:01:46,294 --> 00:01:47,128
‎RESTRICTED AREA

19
00:01:47,211 --> 00:01:48,421
‎EPISODE 12

20
00:01:48,504 --> 00:01:50,590
‎-You all must've been shocked.
‎-Yes.

21
00:01:51,341 --> 00:01:53,051
‎I'll cut to the chase.

22
00:01:53,134 --> 00:01:55,511
‎It wasn't an issue
‎with the transplanted heart.

23
00:01:55,595 --> 00:01:58,223
‎It was hyperventilation
‎caused by excessive stress.

24
00:02:00,516 --> 00:02:01,643
‎Oh, thank you.

25
00:02:01,726 --> 00:02:04,437
‎If he goes into shock
‎and hyperventilates again like today,

26
00:02:04,520 --> 00:02:05,605
‎it could cause arrhythmia.

27
00:02:05,688 --> 00:02:07,482
‎He needs complete rest for now.

28
00:02:08,149 --> 00:02:09,359
‎-Okay.
‎-Okay.

29
00:02:09,901 --> 00:02:11,945
‎-Thank you, doctor.
‎-Thank you.

30
00:02:12,028 --> 00:02:14,614
‎My goodness…

31
00:02:14,697 --> 00:02:16,699
‎That gave you quite a scare, didn't it?

32
00:02:18,534 --> 00:02:19,619
‎It's a relief though.

33
00:02:27,043 --> 00:02:29,128
‎-Gang-uk.
‎-Mr. Ma.

34
00:02:31,005 --> 00:02:32,632
‎What is it? No, keep still.

35
00:02:36,010 --> 00:02:38,596
‎Yeo-ri. What about Yeo-ri?

36
00:02:45,603 --> 00:02:47,355
‎-No, you can't…
‎-Gang-uk.

37
00:02:47,438 --> 00:02:49,983
‎-You can't leave like this, Mr. Ma.
‎-Wait…

38
00:02:52,443 --> 00:02:56,155
‎I'm afraid you should
‎prepare yourselves for the worst.

39
00:03:10,795 --> 00:03:11,629
‎Gang-uk!

40
00:03:31,024 --> 00:03:33,568
‎What if Yeo-ri never wakes up?

41
00:03:33,651 --> 00:03:35,236
‎I feel weird about this.

42
00:03:35,319 --> 00:03:37,488
‎They say life has its ups and downs.

43
00:03:39,157 --> 00:03:41,117
‎To think this would happen to her,

44
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:43,619
‎who seemed so confident
‎at the extraordinary general meeting…

45
00:03:44,954 --> 00:03:45,788
‎It's probably

46
00:03:46,914 --> 00:03:48,666
‎for the best if we stay away, right?

47
00:03:48,750 --> 00:03:50,835
‎There's the issue of her succession,

48
00:03:50,918 --> 00:03:55,006
‎so we should lie low
‎and try to stay under the radar.

49
00:03:58,509 --> 00:04:00,928
‎KOREA BARUM MEDICAL CENTER

50
00:04:07,185 --> 00:04:08,728
‎It's all my fault.

51
00:04:11,731 --> 00:04:12,607
‎If it weren't for me…

52
00:04:13,191 --> 00:04:16,486
‎Why would you say something like that?

53
00:04:16,569 --> 00:04:19,989
‎Ms. Cheon will wake up soon.
‎Try not to worry too much.

54
00:04:20,656 --> 00:04:21,783
‎So Mr. Ma,

55
00:04:21,866 --> 00:04:24,452
‎go home and get some rest.

56
00:04:24,535 --> 00:04:27,497
‎Yeah, take care of yourself
‎so you can look after Yeo-ri.

57
00:04:28,414 --> 00:04:30,208
‎If you end up hyperventilating again,

58
00:04:30,291 --> 00:04:32,377
‎-it could damage your heart.
‎-He's right.

59
00:04:32,460 --> 00:04:35,004
‎I heard arrhythmia can be fatal
‎for heart transplant patients.

60
00:04:35,588 --> 00:04:36,798
‎Gosh, your grandmother

61
00:04:37,799 --> 00:04:38,966
‎must've been so shaken up.

62
00:04:42,220 --> 00:04:43,137
‎You can go on home.

63
00:04:45,306 --> 00:04:47,433
‎Look after yourself, okay?

64
00:04:47,517 --> 00:04:50,395
‎Gang-uk is fine now.

65
00:04:51,979 --> 00:04:56,692
‎Fortunately for him,
‎his transplanted heart wasn't the problem.

66
00:04:57,693 --> 00:04:59,946
‎That heart is such a precious gift.

67
00:05:00,029 --> 00:05:01,989
‎For Ji-hwan's sake,

68
00:05:02,073 --> 00:05:04,492
‎I won't allow anything to happen to it.

69
00:05:05,368 --> 00:05:06,536
‎Yes.

70
00:05:06,619 --> 00:05:09,038
‎You don't have to worry, ma'am.

71
00:05:09,664 --> 00:05:11,707
‎I'll be in touch.

72
00:05:12,250 --> 00:05:14,085
‎Yes. Take care, Ms. Song.

73
00:05:14,669 --> 00:05:15,503
‎Bye.

74
00:05:20,049 --> 00:05:20,883
‎Grandma.

75
00:05:21,926 --> 00:05:23,511
‎Oh, Gang-uk.

76
00:05:23,594 --> 00:05:26,055
‎Was the person who gave me their heart

77
00:05:27,140 --> 00:05:28,891
‎someone named Ji-hwan?

78
00:05:32,228 --> 00:05:33,062
‎Yes.

79
00:05:33,146 --> 00:05:34,647
‎And by Ms. Song…

80
00:05:36,274 --> 00:05:37,942
‎do you mean the lady we had lunch with?

81
00:05:39,735 --> 00:05:41,863
‎Now that it's come to this,

82
00:05:41,946 --> 00:05:43,948
‎I guess I can't keep it from you.

83
00:05:44,907 --> 00:05:46,742
‎The heart you were given

84
00:05:47,743 --> 00:05:52,331
‎belonged to the son of the woman
‎we had lunch with.

85
00:05:57,086 --> 00:05:59,839
‎So the person
‎you always had me pray for at the temple…

86
00:05:59,922 --> 00:06:01,340
‎That was Ji-hwan.

87
00:06:02,008 --> 00:06:02,842
‎Yes.

88
00:06:04,260 --> 00:06:05,636
‎You know CL Group, don't you?

89
00:06:06,512 --> 00:06:09,432
‎Ms. Song is
‎the vice president of CL Group,

90
00:06:09,515 --> 00:06:13,060
‎and Ji-hwan was her younger son.

91
00:06:13,644 --> 00:06:15,354
‎If it's CL Group…

92
00:06:16,814 --> 00:06:18,691
‎then he was Kang Min-hwan's brother?

93
00:06:20,985 --> 00:06:24,405
‎I was in a yacht accident
‎when I was in university.

94
00:06:42,590 --> 00:06:45,468
‎If our lives changed track
‎because of this pendant,

95
00:06:46,510 --> 00:06:47,762
‎then that means

96
00:06:48,888 --> 00:06:50,765
‎Ji-hwan really died because of me.

97
00:06:51,766 --> 00:06:53,643
‎Since it was given to you,

98
00:06:54,810 --> 00:06:56,145
‎you should hold onto it.

99
00:08:34,201 --> 00:08:35,286
‎Jang Eun-ju?

100
00:08:37,913 --> 00:08:39,832
‎Will you please help me?

101
00:09:04,190 --> 00:09:07,109
‎Goodbye, to a better place.

102
00:10:20,558 --> 00:10:21,767
‎I'm here at last.

103
00:10:25,479 --> 00:10:27,398
‎Forgive me for taking so long to come.

104
00:10:27,481 --> 00:10:30,151
‎THE LATE KANG JI-HWAN

105
00:10:30,234 --> 00:10:32,403
‎I thought to myself every morning

106
00:10:33,612 --> 00:10:35,489
‎that I'd live a life…

107
00:10:37,742 --> 00:10:39,702
‎that wouldn't disappoint my donor.

108
00:10:52,757 --> 00:10:53,799
‎I came

109
00:10:54,717 --> 00:10:56,135
‎to return this to you.

110
00:10:57,428 --> 00:10:59,096
‎I heard it belonged to you.

111
00:11:01,056 --> 00:11:02,016
‎The time you gave

112
00:11:02,892 --> 00:11:04,268
‎Yeo-ri and me

113
00:11:05,352 --> 00:11:06,771
‎was a precious gift.

114
00:11:09,482 --> 00:11:10,524
‎Thank you for granting it,

115
00:11:12,026 --> 00:11:13,110
‎and I'm sorry it happened.

116
00:11:15,446 --> 00:11:16,697
‎But now…

117
00:11:18,574 --> 00:11:20,951
‎I'm afraid Yeo-ri will leave me.

118
00:11:24,997 --> 00:11:27,166
‎I want to do anything I can for her…

119
00:11:30,586 --> 00:11:32,546
‎but there's nothing I can do.

120
00:11:34,673 --> 00:11:36,675
‎Then the pendant came to mind.

121
00:11:39,011 --> 00:11:41,305
‎If I were to return it
‎to its rightful owner…

122
00:11:43,432 --> 00:11:45,017
‎then perhaps Yeo-ri might come back.

123
00:11:47,645 --> 00:11:49,355
‎I'm here because I'm desperate.

124
00:11:55,653 --> 00:11:56,737
‎I'm begging you.

125
00:12:00,991 --> 00:12:02,826
‎Please help Yeo-ri come back.

126
00:12:06,247 --> 00:12:07,331
‎Please.

127
00:12:09,291 --> 00:12:10,292
‎Please…

128
00:13:20,696 --> 00:13:22,031
‎Prepare to intubate.

129
00:13:46,472 --> 00:13:47,389
‎Ji-hwan.

130
00:13:50,643 --> 00:13:51,727
‎Hold on.

131
00:13:56,398 --> 00:13:58,150
‎We have a pulse.

132
00:14:02,696 --> 00:14:03,656
‎Thank you.

133
00:14:05,449 --> 00:14:06,533
‎Thank you.

134
00:14:11,330 --> 00:14:12,247
‎Ji-hwan.

135
00:14:15,250 --> 00:14:16,752
‎So we meet again here.

136
00:14:19,463 --> 00:14:20,464
‎I'm sorry…

137
00:14:23,175 --> 00:14:24,343
‎for living

138
00:14:26,178 --> 00:14:27,054
‎in your place.

139
00:14:29,264 --> 00:14:30,641
‎I'm so sorry.

140
00:14:31,141 --> 00:14:31,976
‎Don't be.

141
00:14:33,185 --> 00:14:34,186
‎I told you

142
00:14:34,269 --> 00:14:36,981
‎that I'd die in your place
‎so you can live.

143
00:14:45,280 --> 00:14:46,281
‎Does this mean

144
00:14:47,491 --> 00:14:51,036
‎it's time for me to go where I belong?

145
00:14:52,079 --> 00:14:53,038
‎Yeo-ri.

146
00:14:55,791 --> 00:14:57,084
‎You can't get on this boat.

147
00:15:08,012 --> 00:15:09,638
‎You offered your hand to others.

148
00:15:15,436 --> 00:15:17,855
‎They all came here to repay the warmth

149
00:15:18,522 --> 00:15:19,815
‎you showed them.

150
00:15:24,069 --> 00:15:24,945
‎That warmth

151
00:15:26,071 --> 00:15:28,282
‎is what kept you from crossing over.

152
00:15:31,994 --> 00:15:33,370
‎And more than anything…

153
00:15:42,171 --> 00:15:43,172
‎There are those

154
00:15:44,089 --> 00:15:46,717
‎who will never let go of your hand,
‎no matter what.

155
00:15:51,305 --> 00:15:53,891
‎Those wishing for you to come back
‎more than anything.

156
00:15:57,311 --> 00:15:59,104
‎They're surrounding you with their warmth.

157
00:16:06,070 --> 00:16:07,279
‎Go back, Yeo-ri.

158
00:16:08,655 --> 00:16:09,490
‎Then…

159
00:16:13,786 --> 00:16:14,828
‎what about you?

160
00:16:16,747 --> 00:16:17,664
‎This time,

161
00:16:18,874 --> 00:16:20,000
‎you must go on your own.

162
00:16:23,128 --> 00:16:24,171
‎You've been through a lot

163
00:16:26,131 --> 00:16:27,299
‎because of me.

164
00:16:29,301 --> 00:16:30,844
‎I'll go back to where I belong now.

165
00:16:37,184 --> 00:16:38,060
‎Thank you.

166
00:16:40,604 --> 00:16:42,022
‎Thank you, Ji-hwan.

167
00:16:46,860 --> 00:16:47,694
‎I'm thankful

168
00:16:48,570 --> 00:16:49,571
‎for you too.

169
00:18:03,270 --> 00:18:04,271
‎Yeo-ri?

170
00:18:21,455 --> 00:18:23,123
‎You're back, right?

171
00:19:22,307 --> 00:19:23,892
‎Any news on Cheon Yeo-ri's condition?

172
00:19:23,976 --> 00:19:26,186
‎She's been in a coma for a week.

173
00:19:26,728 --> 00:19:28,939
‎Prosecutor Ma Gang-uk
‎has been staying by her side.

174
00:19:31,733 --> 00:19:32,818
‎What about the police?

175
00:19:32,901 --> 00:19:35,821
‎We've handled the surveillance cameras,
‎and they're not up to much

176
00:19:35,904 --> 00:19:37,489
‎after ruling the driver responsible.

177
00:19:39,533 --> 00:19:42,619
‎Check the guest routes for the memorial
‎and rehearse every step

178
00:19:42,703 --> 00:19:44,121
‎to ensure a smooth process.

179
00:19:44,746 --> 00:19:45,747
‎I'll oversee

180
00:19:46,832 --> 00:19:48,041
‎the final inspection myself.

181
00:19:48,125 --> 00:19:49,001
‎Yes, sir.

182
00:19:59,428 --> 00:20:00,595
‎-Thank you.
‎-Thank you.

183
00:20:04,516 --> 00:20:05,559
‎Help me sit up, Gang-uk.

184
00:20:06,935 --> 00:20:08,937
‎You should lie down a little longer.

185
00:20:09,438 --> 00:20:10,439
‎I feel fine.

186
00:20:11,023 --> 00:20:14,234
‎The doctor said I need to move a bit
‎if I want to recover.

187
00:20:18,822 --> 00:20:20,824
‎I have something to ask you.

188
00:20:22,242 --> 00:20:24,119
‎The site of the car accident.

189
00:20:25,162 --> 00:20:27,331
‎How did you know I was there?

190
00:20:30,167 --> 00:20:31,043
‎Ji-hwan told me.

191
00:20:33,754 --> 00:20:35,380
‎I was able to come back

192
00:20:36,381 --> 00:20:38,091
‎because he sent me back.

193
00:20:40,844 --> 00:20:41,678
‎To tell you the truth,

194
00:20:42,679 --> 00:20:44,348
‎I went to see him too.

195
00:20:45,057 --> 00:20:49,353
‎Ji-hwan was the donor
‎who gave me his heart.

196
00:20:51,188 --> 00:20:53,273
‎I found out by chance

197
00:20:53,357 --> 00:20:54,691
‎while you were unconscious.

198
00:20:58,445 --> 00:20:59,404
‎So Ji-hwan…

199
00:21:02,324 --> 00:21:03,200
‎saved

200
00:21:05,202 --> 00:21:06,953
‎both you and me.

201
00:21:10,624 --> 00:21:12,376
‎I returned the pendant to him too.

202
00:21:13,877 --> 00:21:16,380
‎I had to do something for you,

203
00:21:16,963 --> 00:21:18,924
‎but I just didn't know what.

204
00:21:19,925 --> 00:21:21,426
‎So I thought returning the pendant

205
00:21:22,677 --> 00:21:24,388
‎might help you come back.

206
00:21:26,306 --> 00:21:28,308
‎I guess that's why
‎I was able to come back.

207
00:21:29,434 --> 00:21:30,727
‎Thank you.

208
00:21:32,479 --> 00:21:34,147
‎I'm so glad you're back.

209
00:21:36,108 --> 00:21:39,361
‎I could wish for nothing more

210
00:21:40,654 --> 00:21:41,988
‎as long as you're with me.

211
00:21:58,672 --> 00:22:01,299
‎No, it's fine. Just stay put.

212
00:22:02,759 --> 00:22:03,593
‎It's okay.

213
00:22:07,639 --> 00:22:10,767
‎Dr. Han says you're recovering fast.

214
00:22:12,394 --> 00:22:13,687
‎That's good to hear.

215
00:22:14,479 --> 00:22:16,356
‎Well, Yeo-ri.

216
00:22:17,232 --> 00:22:18,066
‎Yes?

217
00:22:18,150 --> 00:22:21,319
‎Knowing you got hurt
‎trying to save Gang-uk,

218
00:22:21,903 --> 00:22:23,822
‎I feel so terrible.

219
00:22:25,198 --> 00:22:26,450
‎Please don't.

220
00:22:26,533 --> 00:22:28,452
‎One's sincerity comes before

221
00:22:29,286 --> 00:22:30,537
‎any superstition.

222
00:22:31,163 --> 00:22:33,039
‎I've lived to this age
‎and failed to see that.

223
00:22:34,499 --> 00:22:37,711
‎I'm deeply sorry for what I said.

224
00:22:39,087 --> 00:22:40,297
‎You don't have to be, ma'am.

225
00:22:40,380 --> 00:22:46,219
‎I wish for nothing more
‎than for you two to be happy together.

226
00:22:46,303 --> 00:22:47,137
‎I mean it.

227
00:22:47,220 --> 00:22:50,557
‎Good. And delete Shaman Sim's number.

228
00:22:51,224 --> 00:22:53,059
‎I trust you will manage fine now.

229
00:22:53,143 --> 00:22:54,060
‎I do.

230
00:22:56,771 --> 00:22:59,357
‎Why do we have to keep it a secret
‎that you're awake?

231
00:23:01,484 --> 00:23:04,988
‎Something about the accident bothers me.

232
00:23:05,947 --> 00:23:07,282
‎For now, I want Director Lee

233
00:23:07,365 --> 00:23:09,993
‎to step in as Reina Hotel's acting CEO.

234
00:23:11,703 --> 00:23:12,787
‎Trust me on this.

235
00:23:28,011 --> 00:23:30,096
‎-She must be seriously--
‎-Oh, my goodness!

236
00:23:30,180 --> 00:23:32,057
‎What are you doing here, Ha-ri?

237
00:23:32,140 --> 00:23:33,558
‎Why are ‎you‎ here, Mom?

238
00:23:34,184 --> 00:23:36,311
‎-You said you were too busy to--
‎-You traitors.

239
00:23:36,394 --> 00:23:37,812
‎Fancy seeing you both here.

240
00:23:39,064 --> 00:23:41,650
‎You said we should lie low
‎and stay under the radar.

241
00:23:41,733 --> 00:23:44,903
‎What about you?
‎You said it would be best to stay away.

242
00:23:44,986 --> 00:23:45,820
‎Hey.

243
00:23:46,404 --> 00:23:49,532
‎After all, she's in a coma
‎after being hit by a truck.

244
00:23:49,616 --> 00:23:51,701
‎It would look bad
‎if we didn't care at all.

245
00:23:51,785 --> 00:23:55,580
‎And I just felt bad.
‎It felt wrong to ignore her, you know?

246
00:23:56,164 --> 00:23:58,792
‎Exactly. I guess there's a thin line
‎between love and hate.

247
00:23:59,376 --> 00:24:01,544
‎They say blood is thicker than water.

248
00:24:01,628 --> 00:24:04,130
‎And as a fellow parent,

249
00:24:04,214 --> 00:24:06,341
‎I was worried about the chairwoman too.

250
00:24:06,424 --> 00:24:07,467
‎Okay.

251
00:24:07,550 --> 00:24:09,010
‎Since we're here anyway,

252
00:24:09,094 --> 00:24:10,553
‎let's pay her a visit together.

253
00:24:10,637 --> 00:24:11,930
‎You lead the way, Mom.

254
00:24:21,690 --> 00:24:22,607
‎It's okay.

255
00:24:23,900 --> 00:24:25,110
‎We're okay.

256
00:24:35,370 --> 00:24:37,497
‎Is she gone? Is she?

257
00:24:37,580 --> 00:24:40,083
‎Why are we hiding
‎when we came to wish her well?

258
00:24:41,418 --> 00:24:42,335
‎Well…

259
00:24:42,419 --> 00:24:44,629
‎Seeing the chairwoman all of a sudden

260
00:24:44,713 --> 00:24:46,965
‎reminded me of
‎the extraordinary general meeting.

261
00:24:47,048 --> 00:24:49,259
‎I guess I felt guilty for what I did.

262
00:24:49,342 --> 00:24:51,970
‎That's all the more reason
‎we should get on their good books.

263
00:24:52,053 --> 00:24:54,431
‎Man, it was a great opportunity
‎and we ruined it by hiding.

264
00:24:54,514 --> 00:24:56,057
‎You were the first to hide.

265
00:24:56,141 --> 00:24:57,225
‎I was just…

266
00:24:57,309 --> 00:24:59,853
‎He takes after me,
‎so he has fast reflexes.

267
00:24:59,936 --> 00:25:02,230
‎Oh, I don't know.
‎I must've felt guilty too.

268
00:25:02,314 --> 00:25:05,150
‎What now? Do we go in or not?

269
00:25:05,233 --> 00:25:06,901
‎Let me think for a second.

270
00:25:06,985 --> 00:25:08,361
‎We need to calm down first.

271
00:25:11,573 --> 00:25:13,074
‎Anything on the truck driver?

272
00:25:13,658 --> 00:25:15,869
‎He insists he fell asleep at the wheel.

273
00:25:15,952 --> 00:25:18,455
‎Pil-dong.
‎I know for sure he didn't doze off.

274
00:25:18,538 --> 00:25:19,622
‎Right.

275
00:25:19,706 --> 00:25:22,917
‎I read the investigation report,
‎and there weren't any skid marks.

276
00:25:23,001 --> 00:25:23,835
‎See?

277
00:25:24,336 --> 00:25:25,337
‎There's nothing.

278
00:25:25,920 --> 00:25:28,048
‎-Is my bag still missing?
‎-Yeah.

279
00:25:28,715 --> 00:25:31,926
‎Why didn't the cameras work that night?
‎I mean, we're looking into it…

280
00:25:32,010 --> 00:25:33,303
‎Could someone have taken it?

281
00:25:33,386 --> 00:25:35,805
‎There was a cuff link in my bag.

282
00:25:35,889 --> 00:25:37,432
‎Someone could've

283
00:25:38,266 --> 00:25:39,893
‎caused the accident
‎to get their hands on it.

284
00:25:39,976 --> 00:25:43,563
‎So you're saying
‎the person who killed Park Seung-jae

285
00:25:43,646 --> 00:25:45,065
‎was responsible for the accident too?

286
00:25:45,148 --> 00:25:46,399
‎No.

287
00:25:46,483 --> 00:25:48,943
‎I doubt they did it themselves.
‎They must've hired someone.

288
00:25:54,074 --> 00:25:54,991
‎Hey, Yeo-ri.

289
00:25:58,495 --> 00:26:00,497
‎I wish you'd stay
‎in the hospital a bit longer.

290
00:26:01,581 --> 00:26:02,791
‎Are you sure you'll be okay?

291
00:26:03,291 --> 00:26:04,125
‎Yes.

292
00:26:05,043 --> 00:26:08,213
‎I was so close
‎to never coming back home.

293
00:26:08,880 --> 00:26:10,382
‎It feels strange to be back.

294
00:26:10,965 --> 00:26:11,966
‎Sit down carefully.

295
00:26:15,929 --> 00:26:17,347
‎I'm really okay now.

296
00:26:21,726 --> 00:26:22,769
‎How are things?

297
00:26:23,895 --> 00:26:25,313
‎You still don't see ghosts anymore?

298
00:26:27,482 --> 00:26:28,942
‎What about you, Gang-uk?

299
00:26:29,025 --> 00:26:30,652
‎You held my bare hand.

300
00:26:31,653 --> 00:26:32,487
‎I don't see them.

301
00:26:36,658 --> 00:26:37,575
‎Then I guess

302
00:26:39,202 --> 00:26:41,246
‎I won't see them ever again.

303
00:26:43,581 --> 00:26:44,958
‎That's such a relief.

304
00:26:54,300 --> 00:26:57,512
‎I'd like a coffee.
‎It's been a while since I had one.

305
00:26:57,595 --> 00:26:58,805
‎You can't have one, Yeo-ri.

306
00:26:59,389 --> 00:27:02,016
‎The doctor said absolutely no caffeine
‎for the time being.

307
00:27:04,227 --> 00:27:05,311
‎Drink this instead.

308
00:27:13,111 --> 00:27:15,196
‎Just wait until I catch
‎whoever did that to you.

309
00:27:17,740 --> 00:27:20,034
‎It wasn't an ordinary accident, was it?

310
00:27:20,660 --> 00:27:21,494
‎No.

311
00:27:22,370 --> 00:27:24,497
‎Don't you think
‎whoever killed Park Seung-jae

312
00:27:24,581 --> 00:27:26,624
‎is somehow involved in this too?

313
00:27:27,125 --> 00:27:29,335
‎It's likely that Park was killed

314
00:27:29,419 --> 00:27:31,212
‎by the person he tried to blackmail.

315
00:27:31,796 --> 00:27:33,465
‎The yacht accident was 12 years ago,

316
00:27:33,548 --> 00:27:36,968
‎so it's strange that he tried to blackmail
‎after all this time.

317
00:27:37,594 --> 00:27:39,053
‎Do you think he found out something

318
00:27:39,137 --> 00:27:41,848
‎while he was out for the funeral?

319
00:27:41,931 --> 00:27:43,516
‎I traced Park Seung-jae's movements,

320
00:27:43,600 --> 00:27:45,685
‎and he'd gone to his childhood home.

321
00:27:46,227 --> 00:27:48,980
‎It was practically empty
‎since his father lived there alone

322
00:27:49,063 --> 00:27:50,398
‎until his recent death.

323
00:27:51,566 --> 00:27:52,859
‎Did anything noteworthy come up?

324
00:27:52,942 --> 00:27:56,029
‎The police did an initial inspection
‎but found nothing interesting.

325
00:28:01,284 --> 00:28:02,118
‎Yeo-ri.

326
00:28:02,911 --> 00:28:05,705
‎Don't worry too much.
‎I'll take care of it.

327
00:28:07,165 --> 00:28:09,042
‎Just focus on recovering, okay?

328
00:28:09,125 --> 00:28:11,836
‎You should be careful out there, Gang-uk.

329
00:28:12,420 --> 00:28:13,796
‎The culprit's still out there.

330
00:28:15,006 --> 00:28:15,840
‎Okay.

331
00:28:32,315 --> 00:28:34,692
‎We just need to set up the centerpiece,
‎and we'll be set.

332
00:28:35,944 --> 00:28:36,861
‎Okay.

333
00:28:38,613 --> 00:28:39,447
‎Min-hwan?

334
00:28:40,740 --> 00:28:41,574
‎Mother.

335
00:28:48,081 --> 00:28:50,750
‎Aren't you too busy
‎to handle the memorial ceremony?

336
00:28:50,834 --> 00:28:53,503
‎This should be
‎my first priority, and it is.

337
00:28:54,087 --> 00:28:56,464
‎-We're remembering my brother, Ji-hwan.
‎-Right.

338
00:28:57,048 --> 00:29:01,135
‎I'm sure Ji-hwan feels loved
‎even from the other side,

339
00:29:01,219 --> 00:29:04,138
‎with an older brother like you
‎looking out for him.

340
00:29:05,557 --> 00:29:07,016
‎-Shall we take a walk?
‎-Sure.

341
00:29:09,227 --> 00:29:10,061
‎By the way,

342
00:29:11,104 --> 00:29:13,147
‎I'm worried about Yeo-ri.

343
00:29:14,440 --> 00:29:16,401
‎Her grandmother is old and frail.

344
00:29:16,484 --> 00:29:18,278
‎I'm not sure she can handle the stress.

345
00:29:18,778 --> 00:29:21,364
‎Have you paid Yeo-ri a visit?

346
00:29:21,990 --> 00:29:23,199
‎No.

347
00:29:23,283 --> 00:29:24,492
‎I couldn't bring myself to.

348
00:29:26,870 --> 00:29:28,204
‎I understand.

349
00:29:28,788 --> 00:29:31,416
‎Going through something like this
‎is never easy.

350
00:29:32,834 --> 00:29:34,335
‎Oh, excuse me.

351
00:29:37,338 --> 00:29:38,590
‎Hello, Madam Pang.

352
00:29:40,008 --> 00:29:40,842
‎Pardon?

353
00:29:43,970 --> 00:29:45,013
‎Is that so?

354
00:29:47,307 --> 00:29:48,474
‎Yes.

355
00:29:48,558 --> 00:29:51,561
‎You didn't pack things in order,
‎and now I have to reorganize them all.

356
00:29:51,644 --> 00:29:53,521
‎Then just organize it again.

357
00:29:53,605 --> 00:29:55,023
‎You're talking back at me now?

358
00:29:56,274 --> 00:29:57,483
‎That can go in here.

359
00:30:04,365 --> 00:30:06,075
‎You told me to go like it was no big deal.

360
00:30:09,412 --> 00:30:10,914
‎Let's have a team dinner tonight.

361
00:30:10,997 --> 00:30:12,457
‎I'll treat you to Korean beef. How's that?

362
00:30:12,540 --> 00:30:15,501
‎Yes, Korean beef!
‎Investigator Ko, he'll buy us beef.

363
00:30:15,585 --> 00:30:17,587
‎We can eat beef. Home-grown beef.

364
00:30:19,213 --> 00:30:20,548
‎What's up with you?

365
00:30:20,632 --> 00:30:22,508
‎It's not like he'll be gone forever.

366
00:30:22,592 --> 00:30:24,177
‎He'll be back soon.

367
00:30:24,260 --> 00:30:26,179
‎We'll pretend
‎he's just on a long business trip.

368
00:30:26,262 --> 00:30:28,556
‎Keep crying,
‎and we'll get pork rind instead.

369
00:30:29,140 --> 00:30:30,767
‎We're going to
‎the pork rind place tonight.

370
00:30:31,351 --> 00:30:32,602
‎Fine. Korean beef it is.

371
00:30:32,685 --> 00:30:34,103
‎He said he wants Korean beef.

372
00:30:34,187 --> 00:30:35,855
‎-Let's go. Get up.
‎-Let's go.

373
00:30:35,939 --> 00:30:38,983
‎-I'm hungry.
‎-Let's go get some beef.

374
00:30:46,366 --> 00:30:47,784
‎What do you have to say
‎about the accident?

375
00:30:47,867 --> 00:30:50,453
‎I've yet to place a bigger bet.

376
00:30:50,536 --> 00:30:53,122
‎I'll call you if that doesn't work out.

377
00:30:56,501 --> 00:30:57,752
‎Park Seung-jae…

378
00:30:57,835 --> 00:30:59,504
‎I traced Park Seung-jae's movements,

379
00:30:59,587 --> 00:31:01,714
‎and he'd gone to his childhood home.

380
00:31:10,723 --> 00:31:13,226
‎That's not cooked yet.
‎Eat this piece instead.

381
00:31:17,981 --> 00:31:19,607
‎You eat well for a guy
‎who was crying earlier.

382
00:31:19,691 --> 00:31:21,818
‎I mean, it's beef. It's delicious.

383
00:31:21,901 --> 00:31:22,735
‎It is, right?

384
00:31:24,612 --> 00:31:26,072
‎So don't cry anymore, Investigator Ko.

385
00:31:26,155 --> 00:31:27,532
‎Here, cheers.

386
00:31:27,615 --> 00:31:29,242
‎No more tears, okay?

387
00:31:29,325 --> 00:31:30,618
‎-Cheers.
‎-Cheers.

388
00:31:35,790 --> 00:31:37,041
‎-Oh, right. Mr. Ma.
‎-Yeah?

389
00:31:37,125 --> 00:31:39,585
‎Ms. Cheon's much better now, right?

390
00:31:39,669 --> 00:31:40,545
‎Of course.

391
00:31:42,380 --> 00:31:43,840
‎I miss her all of a sudden.

392
00:31:44,590 --> 00:31:45,717
‎Why don't you call her?

393
00:31:45,800 --> 00:31:47,176
‎-Should I?
‎-Yes.

394
00:31:47,844 --> 00:31:50,596
‎I've always wanted to call a girlfriend
‎during a work gathering.

395
00:31:53,266 --> 00:31:54,100
‎Here.

396
00:31:56,144 --> 00:31:57,228
‎Hi, Gang-uk.

397
00:31:57,311 --> 00:31:58,479
‎Are you resting well, Yeo-ri?

398
00:31:59,105 --> 00:32:01,983
‎Yes, of course.
‎I'm getting plenty of rest.

399
00:32:02,483 --> 00:32:04,318
‎You can't overexert yourself, okay?

400
00:32:07,947 --> 00:32:09,866
‎-I just heard something.
‎-What?

401
00:32:09,949 --> 00:32:11,159
‎-Oh…
‎-Are you outside?

402
00:32:11,242 --> 00:32:12,493
‎No, I'm…

403
00:32:13,119 --> 00:32:14,620
‎I came out for a walk.

404
00:32:14,704 --> 00:32:17,749
‎It was probably a car passing by
‎from over the fence.

405
00:32:17,832 --> 00:32:21,169
‎But there aren't many cars
‎that drive by your house.

406
00:32:21,252 --> 00:32:24,589
‎Yes, but one just
‎happened to drive by just now.

407
00:32:25,173 --> 00:32:26,674
‎Accident-prone area ahead…

408
00:32:26,758 --> 00:32:28,051
‎I hear a GPS too.

409
00:32:28,134 --> 00:32:29,552
‎No, you didn't.

410
00:32:29,635 --> 00:32:30,845
‎That was my TV.

411
00:32:30,928 --> 00:32:32,555
‎You just said you were out on a walk.

412
00:32:33,306 --> 00:32:36,392
‎Yes, but I just got back inside.

413
00:32:36,476 --> 00:32:38,644
‎I'd forgotten to turn off the TV.

414
00:32:39,937 --> 00:32:41,981
‎Yeo-ri, you can't risk any aftereffects.

415
00:32:42,065 --> 00:32:44,108
‎So you shouldn't overdo it, okay?

416
00:32:44,192 --> 00:32:45,401
‎-What's wrong with him?
‎-He's so dramatic.

417
00:32:45,485 --> 00:32:47,612
‎I'll feed your fish for you too.

418
00:32:48,196 --> 00:32:49,030
‎Okay.

419
00:32:49,781 --> 00:32:50,865
‎You be careful too.

420
00:32:50,948 --> 00:32:51,908
‎Okay.

421
00:32:58,206 --> 00:32:59,749
‎She worries about me a lot.

422
00:32:59,832 --> 00:33:01,918
‎-Yeah, it seems like it.
‎-It sure does.

423
00:33:02,001 --> 00:33:03,044
‎Goodness.

424
00:33:03,795 --> 00:33:04,629
‎Let's drink.

425
00:33:11,719 --> 00:33:12,887
‎-Pil-dong.
‎-Yeah?

426
00:33:12,970 --> 00:33:15,348
‎Call me as soon as
‎you get anything on Yeo-ri's case.

427
00:33:15,890 --> 00:33:18,601
‎I'd look into it myself
‎if I were in Seoul.

428
00:33:18,684 --> 00:33:22,146
‎I know. I get the feeling
‎that the case is going nowhere.

429
00:33:22,730 --> 00:33:25,483
‎I asked around, but there were no updates.

430
00:33:26,109 --> 00:33:28,236
‎The public sentiment
‎has been pretty strange

431
00:33:28,903 --> 00:33:30,613
‎after Park Seung-jae died.

432
00:33:30,696 --> 00:33:34,534
‎People are saying good riddance,
‎that he deserved to die.

433
00:33:41,624 --> 00:33:42,750
‎Here's an idea.

434
00:33:42,834 --> 00:33:45,002
‎Let's make this
‎our last drink of the night

435
00:33:45,086 --> 00:33:46,754
‎-and call it a night.
‎-Okay.

436
00:33:46,838 --> 00:33:50,550
‎The two lovebirds are worried sick
‎about each other,

437
00:33:50,633 --> 00:33:52,593
‎-so we should cooperate.
‎-All right.

438
00:33:52,677 --> 00:33:53,553
‎There.

439
00:33:53,636 --> 00:33:56,556
‎Besides, you have to start work
‎down south starting on Monday.

440
00:33:57,682 --> 00:33:59,267
‎-Cheers.
‎-We'll call it a night.

441
00:34:02,061 --> 00:34:04,313
‎You're staying with me for round two.

442
00:34:04,397 --> 00:34:05,314
‎Don't be ridiculous.

443
00:34:06,023 --> 00:34:07,984
‎I really need to get home early tonight.

444
00:34:09,861 --> 00:34:11,362
‎Okay, fine. No more tears.

445
00:34:18,286 --> 00:34:21,038
‎I have a feeling there's something here.

446
00:34:48,357 --> 00:34:49,859
‎Seung-jae's camcorder?

447
00:34:49,942 --> 00:34:51,194
‎LIST OF BELONGINGS

448
00:34:51,277 --> 00:34:54,113
‎ELECTRONICS, CAMCORDER, IN GOOD CONDITION

449
00:34:57,783 --> 00:34:59,243
‎It's missing the memory card.

450
00:35:45,581 --> 00:35:46,415
‎Who's there?

451
00:35:48,709 --> 00:35:50,002
‎Gang-uk?

452
00:35:50,086 --> 00:35:51,504
‎Why are you here, Yeo-ri?

453
00:35:52,088 --> 00:35:53,381
‎What about you?

454
00:36:05,184 --> 00:36:08,729
‎Sir, we've completed the preparations
‎for the memorial ceremony.

455
00:36:13,776 --> 00:36:16,946
‎Once I take over, I'll overhaul
‎the Office of Strategy and Planning first.

456
00:36:17,029 --> 00:36:18,990
‎I'll have you transferred there,

457
00:36:19,073 --> 00:36:20,866
‎and you can serve as my control tower.

458
00:36:22,743 --> 00:36:23,786
‎Yes, sir.

459
00:36:23,869 --> 00:36:26,455
‎Thank you for all your hard work.

460
00:36:26,539 --> 00:36:27,707
‎Thank you, sir.

461
00:36:40,594 --> 00:36:43,347
‎-Thank you for coming.
‎-Of course I had to come.

462
00:36:43,931 --> 00:36:46,350
‎You must be busy,
‎yet you've come two years in a row.

463
00:36:46,934 --> 00:36:48,769
‎-Ji-hwan would be so happy.
‎-Min-hwan.

464
00:36:49,645 --> 00:36:51,355
‎-Excuse me.
‎-Sure.

465
00:36:51,939 --> 00:36:53,024
‎Thanks for coming.

466
00:36:53,107 --> 00:36:54,608
‎-Thank you for coming.
‎-Of course.

467
00:36:55,651 --> 00:36:56,485
‎So…

468
00:36:57,778 --> 00:37:00,906
‎I heard there will be
‎a very important announcement today.

469
00:37:00,990 --> 00:37:02,366
‎Congratulations in advance.

470
00:37:05,077 --> 00:37:06,037
‎I'll see you after the memorial.

471
00:37:07,246 --> 00:37:08,748
‎-I'll see you later.
‎-All right.

472
00:37:11,667 --> 00:37:12,960
‎It's true when they say

473
00:37:13,044 --> 00:37:14,795
‎the title makes the man.

474
00:37:14,879 --> 00:37:18,174
‎Don't you think he has
‎the air of a chairman today?

475
00:37:18,257 --> 00:37:19,133
‎Right?

476
00:37:25,097 --> 00:37:25,931
‎Hello.

477
00:37:27,641 --> 00:37:29,560
‎It's been a while, Vice President Song.

478
00:37:31,103 --> 00:37:35,566
‎I hear a lot about you through your son,
‎CEO Kang Min-hwan.

479
00:37:35,649 --> 00:37:38,027
‎Thank you for attending.

480
00:37:38,110 --> 00:37:38,944
‎Of course.

481
00:37:40,112 --> 00:37:42,573
‎Oh, you know my daughter Ha-ri.

482
00:37:43,074 --> 00:37:44,283
‎Hello, ma'am.

483
00:37:44,367 --> 00:37:45,576
‎Welcome.

484
00:37:48,537 --> 00:37:50,498
‎We will now begin

485
00:37:50,581 --> 00:37:53,209
‎the twelfth memorial ceremony
‎for the late Kang Ji-hwan.

486
00:38:03,677 --> 00:38:04,678
‎We're gathered here today

487
00:38:05,429 --> 00:38:07,932
‎to remember my dear brother Ji-hwan,

488
00:38:08,015 --> 00:38:12,019
‎who left us too soon and unexpectedly.

489
00:38:13,270 --> 00:38:16,565
‎Even though it's been a while
‎since he left us,

490
00:38:16,649 --> 00:38:18,859
‎I still can't believe he's gone.

491
00:38:19,527 --> 00:38:21,737
‎Although he was my younger brother,

492
00:38:21,821 --> 00:38:25,783
‎he was sometimes like an older brother,
‎and at other times, like a friend.

493
00:38:25,866 --> 00:38:28,202
‎He was always there
‎as a reliable companion.

494
00:38:28,744 --> 00:38:31,288
‎His presence alone was a great comfort.

495
00:38:32,164 --> 00:38:35,793
‎Ji-hwan left us all
‎with love and memories.

496
00:38:36,293 --> 00:38:38,087
‎That will remain with us in our lives

497
00:38:39,630 --> 00:38:41,173
‎and live on among us.

498
00:38:42,341 --> 00:38:43,342
‎Ji-hwan, my dear brother.

499
00:38:45,553 --> 00:38:46,595
‎I love you.

500
00:38:47,638 --> 00:38:48,639
‎And Mother,

501
00:38:49,890 --> 00:38:50,891
‎I love you.

502
00:38:54,395 --> 00:38:57,606
‎THE LATE KANG JI-HWAN'S
‎12TH MEMORIAL CEREMONY

503
00:39:03,612 --> 00:39:04,488
‎Let's speed up a little.

504
00:39:04,572 --> 00:39:05,489
‎Okay.

505
00:39:15,207 --> 00:39:16,208
‎Yes, I understand.

506
00:39:17,501 --> 00:39:18,377
‎I'm heading inside now.

507
00:39:22,798 --> 00:39:23,632
‎Who's there?

508
00:39:26,552 --> 00:39:27,928
‎Gang-uk?

509
00:39:28,012 --> 00:39:29,221
‎Why are you here, Yeo-ri?

510
00:39:29,722 --> 00:39:31,098
‎What about you?

511
00:39:50,493 --> 00:39:51,368
‎Just a moment.

512
00:39:53,037 --> 00:39:54,079
‎What brings you here?

513
00:39:56,123 --> 00:39:59,877
‎This is a search and seizure warrant
‎for Kang Ji-hwan's death 12 years ago.

514
00:40:14,099 --> 00:40:14,934
‎Today,

515
00:40:15,518 --> 00:40:17,686
‎many of you graced this hall
‎with your presence.

516
00:40:18,479 --> 00:40:25,319
‎I apologize for not being able to
‎thank each of you sincerely in person.

517
00:40:26,070 --> 00:40:26,862
‎Also,

518
00:40:27,988 --> 00:40:30,449
‎I will take to heart
‎the heartfelt condolences

519
00:40:31,283 --> 00:40:32,535
‎you have offered.

520
00:40:36,080 --> 00:40:39,875
‎All of you present are like family to us,

521
00:40:40,459 --> 00:40:43,879
‎so on behalf of CL's chairman
‎who is convalescing in the US,

522
00:40:44,630 --> 00:40:47,424
‎I would like to make
‎an important announcement

523
00:40:47,967 --> 00:40:51,053
‎concerning the future of CL Group.

524
00:40:52,304 --> 00:40:54,223
‎For the long-term future of our group,

525
00:40:54,306 --> 00:40:56,475
‎it is now time for young leadership

526
00:40:57,017 --> 00:40:59,478
‎as well as a new and different vision.

527
00:41:00,479 --> 00:41:03,732
‎So after a thorough discussion
‎with my family

528
00:41:03,816 --> 00:41:05,859
‎and the board of directors--

529
00:41:05,943 --> 00:41:06,944
‎Just a moment, please.

530
00:41:11,490 --> 00:41:12,324
‎Before that,

531
00:41:12,908 --> 00:41:14,702
‎there's something you should see.

532
00:41:15,703 --> 00:41:17,746
‎Yeo-ri. Are you all right?

533
00:41:19,123 --> 00:41:22,042
‎My gosh, I thought she was in a coma.
‎What's she doing here?

534
00:41:22,793 --> 00:41:24,420
‎I found a video

535
00:41:25,546 --> 00:41:28,257
‎that Ji-hwan left before he passed away.

536
00:41:29,300 --> 00:41:30,134
‎Will you see it?

537
00:41:31,427 --> 00:41:32,428
‎Is that true?

538
00:41:32,928 --> 00:41:34,054
‎Ji-hwan did?

539
00:41:35,389 --> 00:41:37,766
‎Ms. Cheon. What do you think you're doing?

540
00:41:37,850 --> 00:41:38,892
‎Min-hwan.

541
00:41:38,976 --> 00:41:39,810
‎Play it.

542
00:41:48,360 --> 00:41:49,361
‎-Ji-hwan.
‎-Min-hwan!

543
00:41:51,030 --> 00:41:51,864
‎Min-hwan.

544
00:41:52,615 --> 00:41:54,450
‎Min-hwan, save me.

545
00:41:55,659 --> 00:41:57,995
‎Min-hwan, what's gotten into you?

546
00:41:58,078 --> 00:42:00,205
‎Min-hwan. No, don't let go.

547
00:42:00,998 --> 00:42:02,625
‎Min-hwan! Don't let go of my hand, okay?

548
00:42:02,708 --> 00:42:04,793
‎Min-hwan, no! No…

549
00:42:16,347 --> 00:42:17,306
‎Secretary Oh.

550
00:42:19,224 --> 00:42:20,142
‎Yes, ma'am.

551
00:42:20,768 --> 00:42:22,686
‎Escort the guests out of the hall

552
00:42:22,770 --> 00:42:25,689
‎and see that they have
‎no difficulty getting home.

553
00:42:26,315 --> 00:42:27,274
‎Yes, ma'am.

554
00:42:27,775 --> 00:42:30,361
‎Today's memorial service has ended.

555
00:42:30,444 --> 00:42:31,487
‎-What?
‎-It's over?

556
00:42:31,570 --> 00:42:33,572
‎Allow us to escort you out of the hall.

557
00:42:34,156 --> 00:42:35,616
‎Please exit through the back door.

558
00:42:36,367 --> 00:42:37,951
‎-What?
‎-Help me escort them outside.

559
00:42:38,494 --> 00:42:39,745
‎Goodbye then.

560
00:42:50,172 --> 00:42:51,173
‎Min-hwan!

561
00:42:53,425 --> 00:42:55,010
‎What did I just see?

562
00:42:55,594 --> 00:42:57,596
‎No… It's not what you think.

563
00:42:58,430 --> 00:42:59,556
‎Ms. Cheon.

564
00:43:00,140 --> 00:43:02,685
‎Where did you find that video?

565
00:43:03,352 --> 00:43:06,438
‎Park Seung-jae had filmed it
‎with his camcorder.

566
00:43:07,856 --> 00:43:10,526
‎I'm so sorry for causing you more pain.

567
00:43:12,861 --> 00:43:14,530
‎You don't believe what you saw, do you?

568
00:43:15,614 --> 00:43:17,700
‎Until that video is authenticated,

569
00:43:18,617 --> 00:43:20,619
‎-lie low, Min-hwan.
‎-Mother.

570
00:43:21,912 --> 00:43:24,206
‎Do you believe Cheon Yeo-ri

571
00:43:24,289 --> 00:43:26,250
‎and a video
‎that could be faked over me?

572
00:43:26,333 --> 00:43:28,085
‎It's not that I believe it.

573
00:43:28,711 --> 00:43:30,087
‎I'm saying we need confirmation.

574
00:43:32,756 --> 00:43:33,674
‎No.

575
00:43:36,301 --> 00:43:37,636
‎You don't believe me.

576
00:43:39,138 --> 00:43:40,347
‎Ever since I was young,

577
00:43:40,973 --> 00:43:42,933
‎you always believed
‎everything Ji-hwan said.

578
00:43:43,434 --> 00:43:44,518
‎So why don't you…

579
00:43:47,646 --> 00:43:49,523
‎ever believe what I say?

580
00:43:49,606 --> 00:43:50,649
‎Min-hwan.

581
00:43:52,818 --> 00:43:54,486
‎I'll prove the truth to you.

582
00:43:59,491 --> 00:44:00,868
‎It's me.

583
00:44:00,951 --> 00:44:04,455
‎Call Attorney Park and have him
‎put together a team of his smartest.

584
00:44:04,538 --> 00:44:07,541
‎Defamation, spreading false information,
‎I'll sue for everything I can.

585
00:44:10,627 --> 00:44:11,712
‎Kang Min-hwan.

586
00:44:15,048 --> 00:44:16,508
‎You still have more?

587
00:44:17,301 --> 00:44:18,719
‎Why did you do it?

588
00:44:19,720 --> 00:44:20,929
‎Just why?

589
00:44:21,555 --> 00:44:22,598
‎How could you…

590
00:44:23,891 --> 00:44:25,809
‎do that to Ji-hwan?

591
00:44:29,521 --> 00:44:31,607
‎I'm sick of hearing his name.

592
00:44:32,816 --> 00:44:34,610
‎Do you even know what my life was like?

593
00:44:35,486 --> 00:44:38,405
‎People like you, born with everything,
‎could never understand

594
00:44:39,031 --> 00:44:41,200
‎what it's like
‎to forever be in someone's shadow.

595
00:44:42,785 --> 00:44:44,828
‎That's how I've lived my whole life.

596
00:44:44,912 --> 00:44:47,247
‎Falling behind,
‎having everything taken away, yearning!

597
00:44:50,167 --> 00:44:52,169
‎So I didn't want anything
‎taken away from me anymore.

598
00:44:53,962 --> 00:44:55,422
‎The company, my mother,

599
00:44:57,508 --> 00:44:58,550
‎and you.

600
00:45:01,595 --> 00:45:02,804
‎But now, even you

601
00:45:03,555 --> 00:45:05,432
‎are coming after all I have?

602
00:45:05,516 --> 00:45:06,433
‎No.

603
00:45:07,726 --> 00:45:09,186
‎I won't give up that easily.

604
00:45:15,734 --> 00:45:16,610
‎That was it?

605
00:45:18,320 --> 00:45:20,239
‎That's why you let Ji-hwan die,

606
00:45:21,823 --> 00:45:23,200
‎killed Park Seung-jae,

607
00:45:24,201 --> 00:45:25,494
‎and caused that truck accident?

608
00:45:26,370 --> 00:45:27,996
‎Do you think that justifies

609
00:45:28,997 --> 00:45:30,707
‎all the things you did?

610
00:45:30,791 --> 00:45:32,334
‎How could you?

611
00:45:34,545 --> 00:45:35,879
‎You only care about yourself.

612
00:45:37,130 --> 00:45:38,173
‎What about Ji-hwan?

613
00:45:39,925 --> 00:45:42,594
‎What about all the years
‎he spent trusting you?

614
00:45:44,096 --> 00:45:47,099
‎Did that mean nothing to you?

615
00:45:48,600 --> 00:45:49,518
‎Did Ji-hwan say that?

616
00:45:51,603 --> 00:45:52,604
‎Is he here right now?

617
00:45:53,605 --> 00:45:54,690
‎Kang Ji-hwan!

618
00:45:56,066 --> 00:45:58,110
‎What did I do that was so wrong?

619
00:45:58,694 --> 00:46:00,737
‎Do you know
‎what I went through because of you

620
00:46:01,697 --> 00:46:03,407
‎and how much I was looked down on?

621
00:46:04,366 --> 00:46:05,409
‎Do you?

622
00:46:05,492 --> 00:46:08,203
‎THE LATE KANG JI-HWAN

623
00:46:21,383 --> 00:46:22,426
‎Kang Min-hwan,

624
00:46:22,509 --> 00:46:24,595
‎you're under arrest
‎for the murder of Park Seung-jae.

625
00:46:24,678 --> 00:46:25,846
‎Listen.

626
00:46:26,638 --> 00:46:27,973
‎What do you think you're doing?

627
00:46:28,056 --> 00:46:30,559
‎What does it look like?
‎We're carrying out official business.

628
00:46:31,059 --> 00:46:33,228
‎While you put on a show
‎planning the memorial,

629
00:46:33,312 --> 00:46:34,896
‎the police found
‎all the relevant evidence.

630
00:46:37,691 --> 00:46:38,692
‎Mr. Ma.

631
00:46:55,667 --> 00:46:56,585
‎Take him in.

632
00:46:58,295 --> 00:47:01,214
‎You have the right to an attorney,
‎the right to defend yourself,

633
00:47:01,298 --> 00:47:03,925
‎-You can't do this. Let me go!
‎-and challenge your arrest.

634
00:47:04,009 --> 00:47:05,344
‎-Hold still.
‎-Let go!

635
00:47:07,512 --> 00:47:10,349
‎Ma Gang-uk, I'll make you pay for this.

636
00:47:10,432 --> 00:47:11,558
‎Got it?

637
00:47:12,184 --> 00:47:13,268
‎Let go of me!

638
00:47:14,144 --> 00:47:15,145
‎Damn it!

639
00:47:16,063 --> 00:47:16,980
‎Ma Gang-uk!

640
00:47:17,648 --> 00:47:18,899
‎It's not over yet!

641
00:47:19,650 --> 00:47:20,942
‎-Let me go!
‎-Are you okay?

642
00:47:21,026 --> 00:47:21,860
‎Hey!

643
00:47:22,361 --> 00:47:23,612
‎Let me go right now!

644
00:47:28,033 --> 00:47:29,368
‎We have a news flash.

645
00:47:29,451 --> 00:47:30,702
‎Kang Min-hwan, CEO of CL Group,

646
00:47:30,786 --> 00:47:34,247
‎was just arrested
‎for the murder of Park Seung-jae,

647
00:47:34,331 --> 00:47:37,751
‎a former pro golfer
‎and son of late Assemblyman Park Jin-dong.

648
00:47:37,834 --> 00:47:39,127
‎The news shocked the public.

649
00:47:39,711 --> 00:47:43,423
‎Despite speculation on the motive
‎and circumstances of Park's death,

650
00:47:43,507 --> 00:47:46,802
‎CL Group has yet to release
‎an official statement,

651
00:47:46,885 --> 00:47:48,512
‎raising further questions.

652
00:47:52,099 --> 00:47:53,517
‎What do you think you're doing?

653
00:47:53,600 --> 00:47:55,811
‎-Director Ok Gye-hui?
‎-Yes, that's me.

654
00:47:55,894 --> 00:47:57,437
‎I'm Prosecutor Im Seo-hyeon
‎from the District Prosecutors' Office,

655
00:47:58,522 --> 00:48:00,273
‎and this is a search and seizure warrant.

656
00:48:00,357 --> 00:48:03,652
‎It took us a while to get past
‎Chief Prosecutor Ok Gye-dong.

657
00:48:03,735 --> 00:48:06,363
‎Director Cheon Dong-jun's office
‎is being searched as we speak.

658
00:48:06,947 --> 00:48:09,032
‎Even Dong-jun? What now, Mom?

659
00:48:09,533 --> 00:48:12,494
‎Excuse me, everyone. Gentlemen?

660
00:48:12,577 --> 00:48:16,123
‎Is the district chief prosecutor
‎aware of this happening?

661
00:48:16,206 --> 00:48:17,749
‎Can you handle the aftermath?

662
00:48:18,333 --> 00:48:19,584
‎We're here because we can.

663
00:48:19,668 --> 00:48:20,752
‎Ms. Im.

664
00:48:20,836 --> 00:48:22,087
‎No, not that!

665
00:48:22,170 --> 00:48:23,922
‎Don't touch that! Leave it alone!

666
00:48:24,005 --> 00:48:25,799
‎You can't touch my safe!

667
00:48:25,882 --> 00:48:28,301
‎You must have something valuable inside.
‎Let's start with this.

668
00:48:28,385 --> 00:48:32,431
‎You'd better hope my safe
‎is on the list of items to be seized.

669
00:48:32,514 --> 00:48:33,974
‎If it's not, you're all done for.

670
00:48:34,933 --> 00:48:36,017
‎Why can't I see the letters?

671
00:48:36,101 --> 00:48:39,396
‎Ha-ri, get my reading glasses.

672
00:48:39,479 --> 00:48:40,313
‎Mom.

673
00:48:40,397 --> 00:48:41,523
‎I can't read a thing.

674
00:48:42,816 --> 00:48:44,192
‎You'd better hope it's on this list.

675
00:48:45,527 --> 00:48:47,863
‎Gosh, why are the letters so blurry?
‎I can't see a thing.

676
00:48:47,946 --> 00:48:49,865
‎Why can't I read a word on this?

677
00:48:50,407 --> 00:48:51,324
‎Why can't I see anything?

678
00:48:51,950 --> 00:48:52,909
‎I still can't see…

679
00:48:53,952 --> 00:48:55,078
‎Mom!

680
00:48:55,162 --> 00:48:56,621
‎No! Mom!

681
00:48:57,497 --> 00:48:58,457
‎Mom!

682
00:48:59,040 --> 00:49:00,459
‎Mom, what's wrong?

683
00:49:00,542 --> 00:49:02,210
‎Stay with me, Mom. Mom!

684
00:49:02,294 --> 00:49:03,420
‎Ha-ri. Mom!

685
00:49:03,503 --> 00:49:05,714
‎Call an ambulance! Mom!

686
00:49:06,757 --> 00:49:13,764
‎1 YEAR LATER

687
00:49:21,396 --> 00:49:23,482
‎Hello, ma'am. How can I help you?

688
00:49:23,565 --> 00:49:24,816
‎I have a reservation.

689
00:49:24,900 --> 00:49:26,067
‎Can I have the name, please?

690
00:49:26,151 --> 00:49:27,360
‎It's Choi Seo-rin.

691
00:49:27,444 --> 00:49:29,488
‎Choi Seo-rin…

692
00:49:29,571 --> 00:49:31,615
‎I need a coffee too.

693
00:49:34,242 --> 00:49:36,703
‎By the way, did you hear the rumor?

694
00:49:37,287 --> 00:49:38,246
‎What rumor?

695
00:49:38,955 --> 00:49:41,958
‎Oh, the rumor
‎that you're being promoted to director?

696
00:49:44,169 --> 00:49:45,545
‎-You heard?
‎-Of course.

697
00:49:45,629 --> 00:49:47,339
‎Weren't you the one who spread it?

698
00:49:47,422 --> 00:49:50,258
‎-It was all over the group chat.
‎-It's already spread that far?

699
00:49:51,593 --> 00:49:52,636
‎That's insane.

700
00:49:52,719 --> 00:49:54,554
‎Why? Isn't that a good thing?

701
00:49:54,638 --> 00:49:57,224
‎Yes, of course it's a good thing.
‎But you know what they say.

702
00:49:57,307 --> 00:49:59,392
‎"He who wants the crown

703
00:49:59,476 --> 00:50:01,269
‎must bear its weight."

704
00:50:02,687 --> 00:50:05,148
‎It's Reina Hotel's director
‎we're talking about.

705
00:50:05,232 --> 00:50:07,734
‎That comes with a huge sense
‎of responsibility and duty.

706
00:50:07,818 --> 00:50:09,653
‎Think of how heavy the weight will be.

707
00:50:09,736 --> 00:50:11,863
‎My shoulders are tensing up already.

708
00:50:12,823 --> 00:50:14,574
‎Just put on some pain relief patches then.

709
00:50:16,618 --> 00:50:18,954
‎Nothing could be heavier
‎than the weight I'm burdened with.

710
00:50:21,623 --> 00:50:22,499
‎Look at me.

711
00:50:23,291 --> 00:50:26,086
‎This is what happens when you lose
‎a power struggle in the royal family.

712
00:50:26,169 --> 00:50:27,754
‎Can you make me a coffee too?

713
00:50:34,511 --> 00:50:36,888
‎Excusez-moi,‎ Ms. Royal Family?

714
00:50:37,764 --> 00:50:41,726
‎I noticed the trash can
‎under the concierge desk

715
00:50:41,810 --> 00:50:43,228
‎was full and overflowing.

716
00:50:43,311 --> 00:50:45,230
‎Would you mind emptying it out?

717
00:50:47,023 --> 00:50:47,858
‎Right now.

718
00:50:50,235 --> 00:50:51,236
‎Okay.

719
00:50:54,948 --> 00:50:56,741
‎-Mom.
‎-Mom.

720
00:50:56,825 --> 00:50:59,202
‎Oh, Ha-ri, Dong-jun.

721
00:51:03,957 --> 00:51:07,127
‎It's hard work
‎being a concierge, isn't it?

722
00:51:08,003 --> 00:51:10,505
‎I'm doing what I'm told
‎and starting from rock bottom,

723
00:51:11,965 --> 00:51:12,841
‎but it's so hard.

724
00:51:12,924 --> 00:51:15,343
‎Hey, Cheon Ha-ri. Look at Mom.

725
00:51:16,094 --> 00:51:17,929
‎You're saying you have it hard
‎when she's in prison?

726
00:51:18,013 --> 00:51:19,890
‎The negligence and embezzlement…

727
00:51:20,515 --> 00:51:22,392
‎You're in here because
‎you took the fall for everything.

728
00:51:22,475 --> 00:51:25,353
‎You got off on probation,
‎so you need to be extra careful.

729
00:51:25,437 --> 00:51:26,646
‎I am being careful.

730
00:51:27,731 --> 00:51:30,025
‎And you, Ha-ri. Remember what I told you?

731
00:51:30,108 --> 00:51:32,736
‎Now that things have come to this, lie low

732
00:51:32,819 --> 00:51:34,362
‎and learn the ropes properly.

733
00:51:34,988 --> 00:51:39,367
‎Make sure that Chairwoman Cheon knows
‎you're working hard and diligently.

734
00:51:40,201 --> 00:51:41,828
‎-"Chairwoman Cheon"?
‎-Yeah.

735
00:51:41,912 --> 00:51:43,288
‎You mean Yeo-ri?

736
00:51:43,371 --> 00:51:47,292
‎Is there anyone else with that surname
‎who happens to be a chairwoman

737
00:51:47,375 --> 00:51:49,628
‎other than Chairwoman Cheon Yeo-ri?

738
00:51:51,129 --> 00:51:52,213
‎Listen.

739
00:51:52,297 --> 00:51:54,257
‎How you speak is a habit.

740
00:51:54,341 --> 00:51:57,969
‎You must practice saying the right thing
‎even when no one is looking.

741
00:51:58,053 --> 00:52:00,347
‎That way, you never make mistakes.

742
00:52:00,430 --> 00:52:02,599
‎Mom, what are you saying?

743
00:52:02,682 --> 00:52:04,976
‎Don't you know whose fault it is
‎that our lives are like this?

744
00:52:05,060 --> 00:52:06,686
‎How can you even call her "chairwoman"?

745
00:52:06,770 --> 00:52:10,649
‎That's in the past.
‎We need to look ahead, all right?

746
00:52:10,732 --> 00:52:13,610
‎Hey, don't you know
‎how many Reina subsidiaries there are?

747
00:52:13,693 --> 00:52:17,572
‎Imagine how busy the chairwoman must be,
‎overseeing the entire group.

748
00:52:17,656 --> 00:52:21,034
‎If you gain the skills
‎and knowledge needed,

749
00:52:21,117 --> 00:52:24,579
‎she might even put you
‎in charge of Reina Hotel.

750
00:52:24,663 --> 00:52:26,247
‎Do you really think so?

751
00:52:26,331 --> 00:52:27,832
‎It's hard to ignore a blood relative.

752
00:52:27,916 --> 00:52:31,586
‎Why do you think your grandma
‎chose Chairwoman Cheon over us?

753
00:52:31,670 --> 00:52:32,545
‎In the end,

754
00:52:32,629 --> 00:52:35,548
‎everyone gives in to blood, got it?

755
00:52:35,632 --> 00:52:36,925
‎You really think so?

756
00:52:37,008 --> 00:52:38,051
‎Of course.

757
00:52:38,134 --> 00:52:41,221
‎So you behave well, Dong-jun.

758
00:52:41,304 --> 00:52:43,932
‎Stay loyal to Chairwoman Cheon, okay?

759
00:52:44,516 --> 00:52:46,101
‎Okay. I'll stay loyal.

760
00:52:53,149 --> 00:52:54,150
‎Yeo-ri!

761
00:53:12,460 --> 00:53:13,878
‎You came here without a call?

762
00:53:13,962 --> 00:53:15,630
‎What are you doing here?

763
00:53:15,714 --> 00:53:18,383
‎-I missed you so much.
‎-So did I.

764
00:53:19,300 --> 00:53:20,719
‎I hope nothing's wrong.

765
00:53:20,802 --> 00:53:22,637
‎So this is what it feels like.

766
00:53:22,721 --> 00:53:23,847
‎What do you mean?

767
00:53:23,930 --> 00:53:26,516
‎You're always springing surprises on me,

768
00:53:26,599 --> 00:53:28,059
‎so I wanted to try it for a change.

769
00:53:29,144 --> 00:53:29,978
‎So how does it feel?

770
00:53:32,814 --> 00:53:34,649
‎It's just the same as any other day.

771
00:53:37,235 --> 00:53:40,780
‎I attended an event
‎at Reina Hotel in Gyeongju.

772
00:53:40,864 --> 00:53:43,658
‎I was supposed to
‎head back to Seoul right after,

773
00:53:43,742 --> 00:53:44,868
‎but I stopped by to see you.

774
00:53:46,077 --> 00:53:48,413
‎We must have some kind of connection.

775
00:53:48,496 --> 00:53:49,581
‎I had something to say.

776
00:53:49,664 --> 00:53:50,582
‎What is it?

777
00:53:50,665 --> 00:53:53,209
‎I'm returning to Seoul. I got promoted.

778
00:53:53,793 --> 00:53:55,754
‎Really? When do you come back?

779
00:53:55,837 --> 00:53:58,423
‎It was announced today,
‎so some time in the next ten days?

780
00:53:59,299 --> 00:54:00,133
‎Really?

781
00:54:02,385 --> 00:54:05,138
‎I'm more pleased
‎that you're happy about it

782
00:54:05,221 --> 00:54:06,723
‎than the fact that I got promoted.

783
00:54:06,806 --> 00:54:08,683
‎Let's go on dates every day
‎once I return to Seoul.

784
00:54:09,434 --> 00:54:10,977
‎-Then tomorrow…
‎-Yes?

785
00:54:11,519 --> 00:54:13,063
‎To celebrate your promotion,

786
00:54:14,064 --> 00:54:16,149
‎how about we go on a date here in Andong?

787
00:54:16,733 --> 00:54:17,984
‎Can we do that?

788
00:54:18,526 --> 00:54:20,820
‎I only got to see you briefly so far.

789
00:54:21,905 --> 00:54:24,449
‎Then I'll take tomorrow off.

790
00:54:24,991 --> 00:54:28,286
‎I'd been meaning to
‎check out a few places here.

791
00:54:28,369 --> 00:54:30,663
‎I held off so I could go with you.

792
00:54:30,747 --> 00:54:32,999
‎-Where?
‎-To see some traditional houses,

793
00:54:33,500 --> 00:54:35,043
‎and maybe a masked dance?

794
00:54:35,627 --> 00:54:36,669
‎We can eat at nice restaurants

795
00:54:36,753 --> 00:54:38,338
‎and see the sunset together.

796
00:54:38,421 --> 00:54:41,341
‎Just thinking about
‎doing all that with you makes me happy.

797
00:54:42,759 --> 00:54:43,593
‎Right now?

798
00:54:43,676 --> 00:54:46,096
‎Right now? Okay. Let's go.

799
00:54:46,179 --> 00:54:47,680
‎-Let's go then.
‎-Okay.

800
00:54:48,765 --> 00:54:50,558
‎How about you get on the back of my bike?

801
00:54:55,313 --> 00:54:56,397
‎-This is fun.
‎-It's fun?

802
00:54:56,481 --> 00:54:57,482
‎Yes.

803
00:54:57,565 --> 00:54:59,234
‎Do I weigh that much though?

804
00:54:59,317 --> 00:55:00,610
‎Why are you going so slow?

805
00:55:00,693 --> 00:55:01,986
‎I'm not.

806
00:55:02,070 --> 00:55:03,696
‎This isn't an electric bike.

807
00:55:04,823 --> 00:55:06,950
‎Are you holding on tight, Yeo-ri?

808
00:55:08,576 --> 00:55:10,203
‎Oh, careful. Careful.

809
00:55:11,162 --> 00:55:14,290
‎CORRECTIONAL SERVICES
‎ADVANCING ORDER AND HUMAN RIGHTS

810
00:55:40,608 --> 00:55:41,609
‎Why did you

811
00:55:42,277 --> 00:55:44,779
‎refuse my visits all this time?

812
00:55:46,447 --> 00:55:48,074
‎Didn't you miss me?

813
00:55:53,079 --> 00:55:54,122
‎I was afraid.

814
00:55:57,292 --> 00:55:59,544
‎I feared the way you'd look at me…

815
00:56:02,630 --> 00:56:04,340
‎now that you know what I did to Ji-hwan.

816
00:56:06,759 --> 00:56:08,970
‎If you don't want to terminate
‎Min-hwan's adoption,

817
00:56:09,596 --> 00:56:11,431
‎send him abroad to study
‎as soon as possible.

818
00:56:12,348 --> 00:56:13,808
‎I've seen many people like him.

819
00:56:14,434 --> 00:56:17,645
‎They bite the hand that fed them
‎once they grow up.

820
00:56:18,354 --> 00:56:21,566
‎Ji-hwan loves his brother.

821
00:56:21,649 --> 00:56:24,819
‎And Min-hwan takes
‎good care of Ji-hwan too.

822
00:56:25,486 --> 00:56:27,822
‎Mother, don't forget that Min-hwan

823
00:56:28,656 --> 00:56:31,326
‎is also a member of this family.

824
00:56:33,369 --> 00:56:34,412
‎I'm sorry.

825
00:56:38,917 --> 00:56:39,751
‎Min-hwan.

826
00:56:42,629 --> 00:56:45,506
‎This is what I think.

827
00:56:47,425 --> 00:56:48,426
‎One day,

828
00:56:49,677 --> 00:56:52,597
‎after you've paid the price
‎for your wrongdoings

829
00:56:53,514 --> 00:56:55,558
‎and are ready to rejoin society,

830
00:56:56,768 --> 00:56:59,437
‎if you have nowhere else to turn to…

831
00:57:01,105 --> 00:57:02,148
‎I think

832
00:57:04,025 --> 00:57:06,444
‎I'd be able to welcome you back.

833
00:57:08,488 --> 00:57:09,822
‎Whenever that may be.

834
00:57:42,897 --> 00:57:44,023
‎Come give me a hug,

835
00:57:44,107 --> 00:57:47,360
‎our new deputy chief prosecutor.

836
00:57:52,407 --> 00:57:53,366
‎You've heard, right?

837
00:57:54,284 --> 00:57:56,703
‎The entire leadership here
‎has been replaced.

838
00:57:56,786 --> 00:57:58,329
‎-So I heard.
‎-Did you also hear

839
00:57:58,413 --> 00:58:01,291
‎that the new prosecutor general
‎picked you out himself

840
00:58:01,374 --> 00:58:02,667
‎to have you work directly for him?

841
00:58:03,793 --> 00:58:05,253
‎He's a great judge of character.

842
00:58:06,588 --> 00:58:07,630
‎I'm so envious.

843
00:58:08,256 --> 00:58:11,593
‎Anyone I side with gets fired,
‎demoted, or whatever.

844
00:58:11,676 --> 00:58:14,345
‎Every connection I make
‎is the worst connection ever.

845
00:58:14,846 --> 00:58:18,016
‎How do you gain powerful connections
‎when you don't do anything?

846
00:58:18,099 --> 00:58:21,311
‎Who said I don't do anything?
‎I work hard, okay?

847
00:58:21,978 --> 00:58:22,895
‎By the book.

848
00:58:23,896 --> 00:58:24,814
‎"By the book."

849
00:58:27,400 --> 00:58:29,986
‎-I'm back!
‎-Long time no see.

850
00:58:30,069 --> 00:58:30,945
‎I said I'm back.

851
00:58:31,029 --> 00:58:33,823
‎-Where did it go?
‎-It must be here somewhere.

852
00:58:33,906 --> 00:58:35,325
‎Why are you ignoring me?

853
00:58:35,408 --> 00:58:36,409
‎This is something important.

854
00:58:36,492 --> 00:58:38,119
‎-Where is it?
‎-What's so important?

855
00:58:38,202 --> 00:58:39,954
‎Where did we put it? Is it behind this?

856
00:58:41,164 --> 00:58:43,708
‎CONGRATULATIONS ON YOUR PROMOTION
‎DEPUTY CHIEF PROSECUTOR

857
00:58:43,791 --> 00:58:45,376
‎Mr. Ma!

858
00:58:48,630 --> 00:58:49,881
‎Careful, careful.

859
00:58:49,964 --> 00:58:52,133
‎-I like your new style.
‎-Deputy Chief Prosecutor!

860
00:58:52,216 --> 00:58:53,635
‎That hairstyle makes you look older.

861
00:58:53,718 --> 00:58:56,929
‎-This look is trending nowadays.
‎-Are you sure about that?

862
00:58:57,013 --> 00:59:00,350
‎It was too short a while
‎to call it a short while.

863
00:59:00,433 --> 00:59:01,351
‎I told you, didn't I?

864
00:59:01,434 --> 00:59:04,562
‎That he'd return with a promotion
‎before his two-year term was up.

865
00:59:04,646 --> 00:59:05,855
‎-That I did.
‎-Mr. Ma.

866
00:59:05,938 --> 00:59:08,107
‎I've lost weight because
‎we haven't had any team dinners.

867
00:59:08,691 --> 00:59:09,942
‎-You sure?
‎-You look the same.

868
00:59:10,026 --> 00:59:12,070
‎I look the same, but I've lost weight.

869
00:59:12,779 --> 00:59:16,282
‎Anyway, let's make up for all the dinners
‎with a party today. Deal?

870
00:59:16,366 --> 00:59:18,618
‎-Deal.
‎-Deal.

871
00:59:18,701 --> 00:59:19,994
‎But before that,

872
00:59:20,078 --> 00:59:21,412
‎we must work.

873
00:59:22,455 --> 00:59:23,581
‎-Okay.
‎-Okay.

874
00:59:23,665 --> 00:59:25,375
‎Now, let's get to it!

875
00:59:26,084 --> 00:59:27,502
‎This is yours.

876
00:59:29,003 --> 00:59:31,964
‎-I'll take… Okay.
‎-Bring those over here.

877
00:59:32,048 --> 00:59:33,675
‎I'll start with this much.

878
00:59:33,758 --> 00:59:34,884
‎Okay.

879
00:59:35,635 --> 00:59:38,721
‎This stack should last us a few years.

880
00:59:38,805 --> 00:59:39,722
‎Don't you think so?

881
00:59:41,766 --> 00:59:42,809
‎What should we eat today?

882
00:59:44,644 --> 00:59:46,604
‎Where should we go for our first round?

883
00:59:46,688 --> 00:59:49,107
‎The Parents' Day Special
‎is being very well received.

884
00:59:49,190 --> 00:59:51,484
‎-Is everything going smoothly?
‎-Absolutely.

885
00:59:51,567 --> 00:59:53,027
‎Everything's going…

886
00:59:56,739 --> 00:59:57,949
‎Are you okay?

887
00:59:58,032 --> 00:59:59,784
‎Oh, dear. I'm sorry.

888
01:00:04,497 --> 01:00:07,208
‎Let's get you up. One, two. There you go.

889
01:00:08,418 --> 01:00:09,252
‎I'm sorry.

890
01:00:09,335 --> 01:00:11,045
‎-It's fine.
‎-Thank you.

891
01:00:11,629 --> 01:00:12,463
‎Take care.

892
01:00:13,047 --> 01:00:14,090
‎Bye.

893
01:00:22,140 --> 01:00:23,266
‎Oh, where was I?

894
01:00:23,349 --> 01:00:25,852
‎-The Parents' Day Special.
‎-Right, let's go.

895
01:00:26,436 --> 01:00:28,062
‎It's good to see you all.

896
01:00:28,146 --> 01:00:30,189
‎INAUGURATION OF REINA GROUP'S CHAIRWOMAN

897
01:00:30,273 --> 01:00:32,191
‎You would agree that Reina Group

898
01:00:32,275 --> 01:00:34,986
‎has been through a lot
‎in the past few years.

899
01:00:35,069 --> 01:00:36,279
‎We've had some tough times.

900
01:00:37,697 --> 01:00:39,824
‎Despite all that,

901
01:00:39,907 --> 01:00:42,994
‎our group has maintained
‎its position at the top.

902
01:00:43,077 --> 01:00:47,373
‎Now, as we are about to
‎take an evolutionary leap,

903
01:00:47,957 --> 01:00:49,876
‎we need a new leader.

904
01:00:50,918 --> 01:00:53,045
‎Someone with a delicate touch and insight

905
01:00:53,129 --> 01:00:57,049
‎who has also proven to be a strong leader
‎and can take action when necessary.

906
01:00:58,176 --> 01:00:59,719
‎I wish to appoint CEO Cheon Yeo-ri

907
01:00:59,802 --> 01:01:02,722
‎as the new chairwoman of Reina Group.

908
01:01:56,692 --> 01:01:58,194
‎-On the day we got engaged,
‎-Yes?

909
01:01:59,403 --> 01:02:02,114
‎do you remember asking me
‎what I wanted to do?

910
01:02:02,198 --> 01:02:03,282
‎Of course I remember.

911
01:02:04,283 --> 01:02:07,662
‎You said you wanted to walk hand-in-hand
‎with the person you liked.

912
01:02:09,413 --> 01:02:13,125
‎I wondered back then
‎whether that day would ever come.

913
01:02:13,835 --> 01:02:17,255
‎But now, the future I dreamed of
‎has become a reality.

914
01:02:17,880 --> 01:02:18,714
‎It has.

915
01:02:20,508 --> 01:02:22,051
‎Back then,

916
01:02:22,134 --> 01:02:24,220
‎something mundane for everyone else

917
01:02:24,971 --> 01:02:28,307
‎felt almost like a miracle to us.

918
01:02:31,018 --> 01:02:31,936
‎So miracles

919
01:02:33,312 --> 01:02:34,772
‎have become our everyday life.

920
01:02:37,900 --> 01:02:39,151
‎Then what should

921
01:02:39,735 --> 01:02:41,445
‎our next miracle be?

922
01:03:46,010 --> 01:03:48,387
‎SPOOKY IN LOVE

923
01:03:49,138 --> 01:03:50,890
‎-Is this the first scene?
‎-Yes.

924
01:03:50,973 --> 01:03:52,183
‎-The main… Okay.
‎-Yes.

925
01:03:53,017 --> 01:03:55,978
‎-I look forward to working with you all!
‎-Okay!

926
01:03:57,980 --> 01:03:58,814
‎Ma'am?

927
01:03:58,898 --> 01:03:59,941
‎Here's the drink…

928
01:04:00,733 --> 01:04:02,234
‎I mean, the information. Darn it.

929
01:04:03,569 --> 01:04:05,655
‎Life is very precious
‎if you think about it.

930
01:04:07,573 --> 01:04:09,033
‎-Darn it.
‎-Hey…

931
01:04:09,617 --> 01:04:10,826
‎Am I being too sensitive?

932
01:04:16,791 --> 01:04:18,125
‎Of course I'll be okay.

933
01:04:22,004 --> 01:04:23,422
‎If you get the case, you'd win…

934
01:04:24,924 --> 01:04:26,926
‎-I'm sorry, let me try that again.
‎-One more time.

935
01:04:27,009 --> 01:04:28,386
‎Act natural.

936
01:04:29,095 --> 01:04:32,556
‎I located the taxi
‎and emailed you the details…

937
01:04:32,640 --> 01:04:33,975
‎Darn it. I'm sorry.

938
01:04:34,058 --> 01:04:35,851
‎Your muscles are so tense.

939
01:04:37,645 --> 01:04:38,646
‎Cut!

940
01:04:44,360 --> 01:04:46,487
‎Don't forget that I have your back.

941
01:04:47,655 --> 01:04:48,990
‎Don't you ever…

942
01:04:49,615 --> 01:04:50,658
‎Got it?

943
01:04:53,160 --> 01:04:55,162
‎Yeo-ri…

944
01:04:57,707 --> 01:04:58,833
‎Let me try that again.

945
01:05:00,876 --> 01:05:02,086
‎But don't let it show.

946
01:05:03,754 --> 01:05:04,714
‎What was it?

947
01:05:06,048 --> 01:05:06,966
‎What is it?

948
01:05:07,800 --> 01:05:08,759
‎Wait, hold on.

949
01:05:08,843 --> 01:05:11,929
‎If you had a time machine,
‎where would you…

950
01:05:13,431 --> 01:05:14,348
‎This is driving me crazy.

951
01:05:21,564 --> 01:05:22,398
‎One more time.

952
01:05:23,983 --> 01:05:25,067
‎Chug it down.

953
01:05:25,151 --> 01:05:27,028
‎Oh gosh, don't spit it out…

954
01:05:30,614 --> 01:05:31,449
‎I need to tuck it all back.

955
01:05:32,116 --> 01:05:33,951
‎Strolling with the man…

956
01:05:37,913 --> 01:05:39,665
‎I love you, Team ‎Spooky in Love‎.

957
01:05:39,749 --> 01:05:40,833
‎I love you.

958
01:05:41,333 --> 01:05:43,377
‎Dear production staff,
‎thanks for all your hard work!

959
01:05:43,461 --> 01:05:44,754
‎-Thank you!
‎-Thank you!

960
01:05:47,715 --> 01:05:49,258
‎PARK EUN-BIN

961
01:05:49,341 --> 01:05:50,885
‎YANG SE-JONG

962
01:05:50,968 --> 01:05:52,511
‎ONG SEONG-WU

963
01:05:52,595 --> 01:05:54,138
‎JO HYE-JOO

964
01:05:54,221 --> 01:05:55,765
‎KIM DO-WAN

965
01:05:55,848 --> 01:05:57,391
‎YE SOO-JUNG

966
01:05:57,475 --> 01:05:59,018
‎CHA MI-KYEONG

967
01:05:59,101 --> 01:06:00,644
‎KIM SO-RA

968
01:06:00,728 --> 01:06:02,271
‎LEE JUN-HYEOK

969
01:06:02,354 --> 01:06:03,898
‎BAIK JI-WON

970
01:06:03,981 --> 01:06:05,524
‎LEE CHANG-HOON

971
